OL,3,GNEWSAFly-tipping left on road for more
OL,4,Athan a year
OL,5,
OL,6,FFour yellow skips, red sofas, old
OL,7,Fmattresses and bin bags, have all been
OL,8,Fleft on the side of a residential road
OL,9,Fin Moseley, Birmingham, for more than a
OL,10,Fyear.
OL,12,FThe fly-tipping, which started after
OL,13,Fthree Houses of Multiple Occupancy
OL,14,F(HMO) were shut down, has left
OL,15,Fresidents on Park Road unable to sleep,
OL,16,Fout of fear that it might be set
OL,17,Falight.
OL,23,APub: 12-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,352,350,200,160,0,100
PN,35102
SC,0002
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F351A1791786354
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+ js17kjc15 js57kj#4
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-. *,$%**,%-,* %%**,! ,$A(W)
OL,3,GNEWSAFly-tipping left on road for more
OL,4,Athan a year
OL,5,
OL,6,FLocal resident and community activist,
OL,7,FBen Hallam, said: "It's a fire risk.
OL,8,FAll it takes is a cigarette or
OL,9,Fsomething to go there, and the whole
OL,10,Fplace could go up. This is all
OL,11,Fflammable material in the skips and
OL,12,Fsofas."
OL,14,FOn the same day the BBC contacted
OL,15,FBirmingham City Council, the
OL,16,Ffly-tipping was removed from the
OL,17,Fpavement, and the authority said it had
OL,18,Fremoved rubbish from the area
OL,19,Fpreviously.
OL,23,APub: 12-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG2/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (W) NewsCReg TVFWeather
